</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 04, 2005 - 4:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->So Btk would not know what they looked like.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12641-->
<!--Post: 12642--><!--Time: 1112659701-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12642"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 04, 2005 - 5:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that the olny Photos of the children that the police might have are of the  crime scean &amp; that will probely never been released to the public. If there are any regular photo&#39;s of the children, the police probley took those also.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12642-->
<!--Post: 12648--><!--Time: 1112678203-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12648"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 04, 2005 - 10:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry, wrong kids<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12648-->
<!--Post: 12655--><!--Time: 1112702181-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12655"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 05, 2005 - 4:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just read that police took all photos from the house, and Charlie doesnt even have photos of his family.  Makes me sick when I hear that thier dog was put down, and the kids werent even allowed to <BR>have pics from the house. <BR>Who would I contact on Charlies behalf to get him his pictures back?  Or someone local, would anyone <BR>like to make a few phonecalls? <BR> <BR>Or Tom, he may have some pull there.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12655-->
<!--Post: 12663--><!--Time: 1112713803-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12663"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 05, 2005 - 8:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe they were trying to be respectful; or they did not want to upset parents of other children in Wichita; they did not want the killer&#40;s&#41; to come back and retrieve pics of other members of the family and target them; they were trying to prevent the press from getting them; perhaps they thought that the pics would inflame the public and start mass hysteria; they wanted to control the crime scene and more easily determine if it had been breeched. Or, they thought that they would sew the case up quickly and there was no need to show the pics. It could be that someone could have remembered seeing the children talking to BTK and might have provided a clue. I would not be surprised that BTK even contacted some of his victims by phone and did a telephone ruse prior to killing them. Just to gain the excitement of hearing their voices, knowing that they would soon be his. Some surviving family may remember odd or funny phone calls reported by the victims. Of course, a long time has transpired. <BR> <BR>Charlie could file suit and request that his property be returned. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12663-->
<!--Post: 12675--><!--Time: 1112735603-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12675"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 05, 2005 - 2:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe the police took all the photos cause they feared someone might break into the house &amp; steal them &amp; everything eles that was left? I do not even think that the 3 other children got to go back into the house after the murder &amp; get there stuff, did they?  <BR> <BR>The olny people I can think of someone contacting is robert &#40;author of BTK book&#41; or the cops who would have the stuff.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12675-->
<!--Post: 12705--><!--Time: 1112881339-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12705"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 6:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Itty: <BR> <BR>Under Kan. law, items seized by the police &#40;with or without a warrant&#41; become property of the court and can only be released by a court order after they are no longer needed as evidence.  That won&#39;t happen until after the Rader case is over. <BR> <BR>Phoenix<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12705-->
<!--Post: 12708--><!--Time: 1112886970-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12708"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 8:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nancy Fox&#39;s mother doesn&#39;t have many pictures of her daughter left either.  she is not allowed to have her photo albums back.  What good are they to police now.  I think it sucks. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
